<section id="intro">
  <HeroTag text="Training Walkthrough · August 2026" />
  <h1>Getting Started with OLSP Academy: What You Learn in the First 8 Minutes</h1>

  <p>You paid your $7. You're staring at a dashboard full of links, levels, courses, and numbers. <strong>What do you actually do first?</strong></p>

  <p>The answer is one eight-minute video. It's called Getting Started, and the platform itself labels it "Step 1." But nobody tells you what's inside before you click play. This article fixes that.</p>
</section>

<section id="what-it-is">
  <h2>What Getting Started Actually Covers</h2>

  <p>The Getting Started course is the shortest training in OLSP's Skill Center — just under eight minutes. It lives under the Megalink level, which means it's available to every member the moment they join. No upgrade required.</p>

  <p>According to OLSP's own description, the course teaches <strong>"how to make the most out of the system and your mega link."</strong> That's the official promise. Here's what that actually means, broken down:</p>

  <Callout type="info">
    <strong>What you learn in 8 minutes:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Where everything is inside the dashboard — navigation, affiliate section, training library</li>
      <li>What the Mega Link actually is and where to find yours</li>
      <li>How to share your link and what happens when someone clicks it</li>
      <li>The basic commission structure — what you earn and when</li>
      <li>What to do immediately after finishing the video</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>

  <p>It is not a deep dive. It does not teach you Facebook ads, list building, or advanced traffic strategies. It is exactly what the title says: getting started. An orientation.</p>
</section>

<section id="key-lessons">
  <h2>The Key Lessons</h2>

  <h3>1. The Mega Link is your only tool — and that's the point</h3>

  <p>Every affiliate program gives you a link. OLSP gives you one link and builds the entire system around it. You don't need multiple links for multiple products. You don't need to track which link goes where. One link handles everything — and the training shows you exactly where to find it and how it works.</p>

  <p>This simplicity is intentional. Beginners drown in options. OLSP removes the options.</p>

  <h3>2. The dashboard is simpler than it looks</h3>

  <p>First-time login is overwhelming. The Getting Started video walks you through the three things that actually matter on day one: your link, the training library, and the affiliate dashboard. Everything else can wait.</p>

  <h3>3. Your first task is not selling — it's watching</h3>

  <p>The training explicitly tells you not to rush out and start sharing your link. Your first real task is the next course: Getting Started with the Megalink (43 minutes). The 8-minute version gets you oriented. The 43-minute version teaches you how to actually earn.</p>

  <Callout type="warn">
    <strong>Don't skip this step.</strong> The people who earn nothing inside OLSP are almost always the ones who never completed the beginner training. They jump straight to sharing their link — without understanding the system — and quit when nothing happens.
  </Callout>
</section>

